Normal work begins!

This week was my first week out of training. It still feels a little like training as I try to get a grip on everything that is going on. But life is starting to roll and it is exciting. I have officially moved into a flat with my flat-mate Miguel. (“flat” is basically “apartment” in this part of the world. Pictures coming as soon as we get the place in order. ^_^ ) Miguel is the new cook here. He has a big heart for caring for people and prays over every meal he makes. He’s going to be an amazing fellow to live with.

Dance track has begun this week. It is the period in which we train students for four months to prepare them to do ministry through dance. OM-Lh is right now on the forefront of OM-Arts. We are the first full-time dance ministry in OM and so it is an exciting time of trailblazing to see how dance ministry works in this context. Amy, my leader, has talked about times they have danced in churches and for youth conferences and more. There are currently four of us in the main group. We learn both various dances and dance styles. But we are also learning a lot about art in the way God wanted it. We have a creative God. It is really awesome seeing just how much He enjoys seeing our work.

Prayer requests:

    The three school boys and the seeds planted in them.
    Several of the new people have been sick recently – getting used to the little bugs of the UK. God blessed me with only one day of sickness. Pray for the health of the new team members.
    Praise God for the wonderful living arrangement. The flat that God provided is wonderful. The wife of the couple who lived here last was one of the visual artists in the arts ministry here. There are verses painted on a couple walls. It is a real blessing.
    Praise and a request. I came so close to having my support goal before I left that they let me come even though I wasn’t fully supported. I was about $200 short in monthly support. Since I left for the UK, God has provided about half of that! So praise God for the support he has already provided, and pray that the last of it will come in soon.

 

Please let me know how I can be praying for you!

God bless

~Toby

